{"type":"compaction_end","reason":"threshold","result":{"summary":"## Goal\nImplement a 3D office building simulation running entirely in the browser using Three.js 0.147.0 loaded from a CDN, with no build process. The simulation must feature persistent agents pursuing human goals on a simulated clock (arriving for work, sitting at desks, getting up for meetings/chats, breaking for lunch, drifting home around 5 PM) and a realistically-scheduled elevator car ferrying them up and down with proper call buttons, direction handling, and a hard capacity limit.\n\n## Constraints & Preferences\n- **Workspace & Checker Paths**: Workspace is `C:\\Users\\Jeff\\Code\\llm-eval\\evals\\pi_swift-1_5-qwen3_8-flash-next-gsq-rco-abliterated_office_prompt_v3`. Checker scripts (`static_check.js` and `runtime_check.js`) are located two directories above the workspace.\n- **Required Files**: Must create exactly six JavaScript files plus an HTML shell: `person.js`, `world.js`, `elevator_logic.js`, `elevator.js`, `sim.js`, `elevator_logic_test.js`, and `index.html`.\n- **Hard Browser-Load Requirements**: \n  - No ES modules (`import`/`export`) in browser simulation files; use browser globals attached to `window` (e.g., `window.createPerson = createPerson`).\n  - `elevator_logic.js` is the only dual-environment file, using an IIFE pattern for both `window.ElevatorLogic` and Node's `module.exports`.\n  - The simulation must auto-start on page load via a specific `DOMContentLoaded` check in `sim.js`.\n  - Zero startup console errors; no `file://` URLs or self-embedding tags.\n- **Coordinate Conventions**: `+Y` is up, `+Z` is the front of the building (entrance side), `+X` is right. Floor `N` has its walkable floor at world `y = N * FLOOR_HEIGHT`. The shaft is a 3x3 column centered at `x=0, z=0`.\n- **Behavioral & Visual Fidelity**: Emphasis on behavioral fidelity (real elevator scheduling, real office worker behavior). Modest visual fidelity using simple Three.js primitives with semi-transparent surfaces (`depthWrite: false`, `side: DoubleSide`). \n- **Anti-Bunching & Orientation Rules**: Prevent agents from bunching up or getting blocked by the front door, elevator doors, other people, or obstacles. Ensure seated figures are positioned with legs directed toward the desk and away from the backrest (requires a separate system for tracking furniture direction).\n- **Verification Steps**: Must run `node ../../static_check.js .` and `node ../../runtime_check.js .` before finishing to fix any reported issues. Must also run `node elevator_logic_test.js` to verify deterministic Node tests for the elevator logic.\n\n## Progress\n### Done\n- [x] Listed contents of current workspace directory (`ls -la`).\n- [x] Listed contents of parent directory two levels up (`ls ../..`) to locate checker scripts.\n- [x] Read `CHAT_SESSION.TXT`, `PI_EVENTS.JSONL` (first 5 lines), and `SERVER.LOG` (last 20 lines) to inspect session logs and environment variables.\n- [x] Verified Playwright installation (`pw ok`) and Node version (`v24.14.1`).\n- [x] Analyzed `PI_EVENTS.JSONL` structure, identifying event types (`message_end`, `tool_execution_start/end`, etc.) and confirming the session ID (`01a12858-2a16-70f0-abab-f70f58008505`).\n- [x] Inspected `static_check.js` logic, including keyword sets, known globals, string/comment stripping, tokenization, and scope handling.\n- [x] Inspected `runtime_check.js` logic, including Playwright setup, canvas snapshotting, animation frame counting, and timeout handling.\n- [x] Identified that the current workspace directory is empty of required simulation files (only contains logs).\n\n### In Progress\n- [ ] Create the required JavaScript files (`person.js`, `world.js`, `elevator_logic.js`, `elevator.js`, `sim.js`, `elevator_logic_test.js`) and `index.html`.\n- [ ] Implement the elevator logic, agent behavior, and 3D rendering.\n\n### Blocked\n- None currently; ready to begin implementation.\n\n## Key Decisions\n- **No prior history**: The conversation started with exploration of the environment and checker scripts before any code was written.\n- **Checker Script Logic**: `static_check.js` enforces specific script loading order in `index.html` for elevator prompts (Three.js, OrbitControls, `person.js`, `elevator.js`) and checks for duplicate top-level lexical declarations across files. `runtime_check.js` uses Playwright to verify canvas rendering, animation frames, and object counts without blocking the event loop.\n\n## Next Steps\n1. Create `index.html` with the required script loading order (Three.js CDN, OrbitControls, `person.js`, `elevator.js`).\n2. Implement `world.js` for scene setup, lighting, camera, and building geometry.\n3. Implement `person.js` for agent behavior, pathfinding, and animation states.\n4. Implement `elevator_logic.js` (dual-environment IIFE) for elevator scheduling and state management.\n5. Implement `elevator.js` for rendering the elevator car and doors based on logic from `elevator_logic.js`.\n6. Implement `sim.js` to tie everything together, handle the simulation loop, and auto-start on `DOMContentLoaded`.\n7. Create `elevator_logic_test.js` with deterministic Node tests for the elevator logic.\n8. Run `node ../../static_check.js .` and fix any reported issues (especially duplicate declarations).\n9. Run `node ../../runtime_check.js .` to verify browser execution, canvas rendering, and animation frames.\n\n## Critical Context\n- **Workspace & Checker Paths**: Workspace is `C:\\Users\\Jeff\\Code\\llm-eval\\evals\\pi_swift-1_5-qwen3_8-flash-next-gsq-rco-abliterated_office_prompt_v3`. Checkers are in the parent directory (`../../`).\n- **Required Files**: Must create exactly six JavaScript files plus an HTML shell: `person.js`, `world.js`, `elevator_logic.js`, `elevator.js`, `sim.js`, `elevator_logic_test.js`, and `index.html`.\n- **Hard Browser-Load Requirements**: \n  - No ES modules (`import`/`export`) in browser simulation files; use browser globals attached to `window` (e.g., `window.createPerson = createPerson`).\n  - `elevator_logic.js` is the only dual-environment file, using an IIFE pattern for both `window.ElevatorLogic` and Node's `module.exports`.\n  - The simulation must auto-start on page load via a specific `DOMContentLoaded` check in `sim.js`.\n  - Zero startup console errors; no `file://` URLs or self-embedding tags.\n- **Coordinate Conventions**: `+Y` is up, `+Z` is the front of the building (entrance side), `+X` is right. Floor `N` has its walkable floor at world `y = N * FLOOR_HEIGHT`. The shaft is a 3x3 column centered at `x=0, z=0`.\n- **Behavioral & Visual Fidelity**: Emphasis on behavioral fidelity (real elevator scheduling, real office worker behavior). Modest visual fidelity using simple Three.js primitives with semi-transparent surfaces (`depthWrite: false`, `side: DoubleSide`). \n- **Anti-Bunching & Orientation Rules**: Prevent agents from bunching up or getting blocked by the front door, elevator doors, other people, or obstacles. Ensure seated figures are positioned with legs directed toward the desk and away from the backrest (requires a separate system for tracking furniture direction).\n- **Verification Steps**: Must run `node ../../static_check.js .` and `node ../../runtime_check.js .` before finishing to fix any reported issues. Must also run `node elevator_logic_test.js` to verify deterministic Node tests for the elevator logic.","firstKeptEntryId":"985fd5f8","tokensBefore":49375,"estimatedTokensAfter":26761,"usage":{"input":14682,"output":1760,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":16442,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"details":{"readFiles":[],"modifiedFiles":[]}},"aborted":false,"willRetry":false}
